<Base title="About | FULL TIME" description="About FULL TIME, the World Cup 2026 football blog covering every match, player, and story from the tournament.">
  <main style="max-width:740px;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem 1.25rem 4rem;">
    <h1 style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif;font-size:2.5rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">About FULL TIME</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--c-muted);margin-bottom:2rem;">The World Cup, told properly.</p>

    <p>FULL TIME is a football blog built around the FIFA World Cup 2026, hosted across the United States, Canada, and Mexico. We cover every match, every player, and every story worth telling from the biggest football tournament on earth.</p>

    <p>The site was built by Benjamin Gathuku, a software developer and football writer based in Nairobi, Kenya. The goal was simple: bring sharp, well-written football journalism to readers who follow the game seriously, without the noise and clickbait that fills most sports sites.</p>

    <h2 style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif;margin-top:2rem;">What we cover</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>World Cup 2026 match reports and previews</li>
      <li>Player profiles and career retrospectives</li>
      <li>Tactical analysis and statistics</li>
      <li>World Cup history going back to 1930</li>
      <li>International football including the UEFA Nations League</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif;margin-top:2rem;">Contact</h2>
    <p>For editorial enquiries, corrections, or partnership discussions, reach us at <a href="/contact">our contact page</a> or directly at <a href="mailto:benjamingathukumuthoni@gmail.com">benjamingathukumuthoni@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <h2 style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif;margin-top:2rem;">Editorial standards</h2>
    <p>Every article on FULL TIME is written by a human author, fact-checked against primary sources, and updated when facts change. We correct errors promptly. If you spot something wrong, please get in touch.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
